nt of bipolar i depression</article-title><source>Journal of Clinical Psychiatry</source><volume>67</volume><fpage>1025</fpage><lpage>33</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16889444</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b12-ndt-3-579"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Brown</surname><given-names>JB</given-names></name><name><surname>Nichols</surname><given-names>GA</given-names></name><name><surname>Glauber</surname><given-names>HS</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Ten-year follow-up of antidiabetic drug use, nonadherence, and mortality in a defined population with type 2 diabetes mellitus</article-title><source>Clin Ther</source><volume>21</volume><fpage>1045</fpage><lpage>57</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10440626</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b13-ndt-3-579"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bymaster</surname><given-names>FP</given-names></name><name><surname>Rasmussen</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Calligaro</surname><given-names>DO</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1997</year><article-title>In vitro and in vivo biochemistry of olanzapine: a novel, atypical antipsychotic drug</article-title><source>Journal of Clinical Psychiatry</source><volume>58</volume><issue>Suppl 10</issue><fpage>28</fpage><lpage>36</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9265914</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b14-ndt-3-579"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Callaghan</surname><given-names>JT</given-names></name><name><surname>Bergstrom</surname><given-names>RF</given-names></name><name><surname>Ptak</surname><given-names>LR</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Olanzapine: pharmacokinetic and pharmacodynamic profile</article-title><source>Clinical Pharmacokinetics</source><volume>37</volume><fpage>177</fpage><lpage>93</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10511917</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b15-ndt-3-579"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Casey</surname><given-names>DE</given-names></name></person-group><year>1997</year><article-title>The relation of pharmacology to side effects</article-title><source>J Clin Psychiatry</source><volume>58</volume><issue>Suppl 10</issue><fpage>55</fpage><lpage>62</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9265918</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b16-ndt-3-579"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>deLeon</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Armstrong</surname><given-names>SC</given-names></name><name><surname>Cozza</surname><given-names>KL</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>The dosing of atypical antipsychotics</article-title><source>Psychosomatics</source><volume>46</volume><fpage>262</fpage><lpage>73</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15883149</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b17-ndt-3-579"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Doucette</surname><given-names>DE</given-names></name><name><surname>Grenier</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Robertson</surname><given-names>PS</given-names></name></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>Olanzapine-induced acute pancreatitis</article-title><source>The Annals of Pharmacotherapy</source><volume>34</volume><fpage>1128</fpage><lpage>31</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11054978</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b18-ndt-3-579"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fagiolini</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Kupfer</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Houck</surname><given-names>PR</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Obesity as a 